    "body": "Triage of the three screenshots (v0.20.0, build 85da3408, model `Block`, tool EM8, Source: Stock).\n\n**Screenshot 1: one open edge, Side = Inside, no boundary**\n- The selection is `Chain Block · open · 50.0 mm · 1 of 1`: one straight edge, an open run.\n- The page shows the hint \"Side does not apply to open runs - the cutter rides the run's line\". The Side value is ignored on purpose for an open run. The tool centre line is on the edge.\n- The operation generates: `OK · 12 moves · 1 warning`. The warning is \"move 8 cuts past the finish surface - repeated on 2 more moves (to 10)\".\n- Result: the gouge check finds the cut into the part. The operation status stays `ok` with warnings. The screenshot does not show if the post is refused. The worker must confirm this.\n- Defect: an open run has no side. The maintainer expects the tool centre line one tool radius from the edge. An open run needs a left or right side in the direction of travel, or a refusal by name. A silent centre-line pass into the part is not correct.\n\n**Screenshot 2: the same edge as boundary 1 (Include)**\n- Refused by name: \"boundary 1 (Include) is an open chain (1 edge, open chain) - an include / exclude must enclose an area: Shift-click or 'Extend to loop' to close it, or set its role to Open\".\n- No toolpath is made. The operation is `STALE`. This is a refusal, not wrong output.\n\n**Screenshot 3: the vertical wall face as boundary 1 (Include)**\n- Refused by name: \"face 0xe41de48d5aae21f9 of 'Block' projects to a line from above and bounds no area; select a horizontal face or a closed edge chain around the part\".\n- No toolpath is made. This is a refusal, not wrong output.\n\n**Scope after triage**\n- This issue: the side of a Contour on an open run (screenshot 1), and the proof that the pass in screenshot 1 cannot post.\n- Screenshots 2 and 3 show the boundary limits that issue #1727 tracks (an edge as a boundary; draft PR #1756). The open-edge band of issue #1735 (PR #1769) is related. This issue does not repeat that work.\n- Priority stays `P1` until a test shows that the post refuses the pass of screenshot 1. If the post refuses it, the defect is `P3` by the table.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
