    "body": "Reproduction (headless, worker issue-worker-high, branch `issue/1777-contour-side`).\n\nFixture: a 40 x 40 x 10 mm block, centred at the origin. Tool radius 5 mm. Contour from Z 10 to Z 0.\n\nResults:\n- Closed rim (4 edges), Side Auto or Outside: the tool centre runs one radius outside the block (x and y from -25 to 25). There are no warnings. The post is written.\n- One open edge (the north edge, y = 20), Side Auto, Inside or Outside: all three give the same path. The tool centre rides ON the edge (y = 20, no offset). The verify gives `Gouge` at moves 5 and 6.\n- Two open edges (north and east): the same centre ride, 6 warnings.\n- Open runs together with any Boundary control (containment, offset, extra boundary): the generator refuses by name. This is the current law.\n\nIs the post blocked? Yes. For the one open edge, the post refuses with this message:\n\n`post blocked - gouge: program cuts below the model in 512 cell(s), worst 10.00 mm at (-19.69, 15.31, z 0.00)`\n\nFor the two open edges, the post refuses with 960 cells, worst 10.00 mm. Thus the gouge gate stops the wrong pass. No G-code with the gouge goes out. The defect is that the Side parameter has no effect on an open run: the generator always puts the tool centre on the run line.\n\nPlan for the fix: an open run is cut on its air side. The generator reads the part material beside the run at each cut level. Then it moves the tool centre one tool radius (plus stock to leave) to the side with no material. If the part has material on both sides, or the sides do not agree between levels, the generator refuses by name. The rule goes into `docs/decisions/1777-contour-open-run-side.md`.\n\nThe priority label stays as it is. A change of priority is the decision of the maintainer.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
